From ccfe43cb03b08cec002bf656a353842c89a4ae58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/19] feat(core): trimmed write receipts with output: full;
 scale results state the change (C3, C25)

Write results echoed every written object in full: spec, data and the
API's defaults. On the usability pass that was 6,233 tokens of echoes
(first native series) and 2,333 more in the second, almost none of
which the agent used. resources_scale had the opposite problem: scaling
to zero answered `spec: {}` (the API omits a zero) with the status from
before the change, so the result could not show what happened, and the
agent spent two verification reads.

Receipts (C3):
- resources_create_or_update and pods_run return, for each object,
  apiVersion, kind and metadata.name, namespace, uid, resourceVersion
  and generation (and deletionTimestamp if set). That is what a caller
  needs to refer to the object again or to send a version
  precondition. Receipts carry no spec, data, status or secrets.
- A new optional `output` argument, 'receipt' (default) or 'full',
  returns the whole objects as before. The first result line is
  unchanged; a second comment line says how to get the full objects.

Scale results (C25):
- A changed scale is stated as "<Kind> <ns>/<name> scaled:
  spec.replicas <from> -> <to>", and says that the status shown was
  read with the change, before the controller acted.
- spec.replicas is always present, including 0.
- The body is a trimmed Scale (identity, spec.replicas,
  status.replicas); `output: full` returns the whole Scale object.

The default is a deliberate change of output. Tests that inspected full
pods_run objects now pass `output: full`; the resources_scale tests
decode the same YAML as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
